From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:25:02 +0000
Subject: Use an ephemeral profile for Auth Tabs in incognito modes

Auth Tabs, the custom tabs that apps open for a sign-in flow, used the
regular profile unless the app asked for ephemeral browsing, even when the
link was otherwise treated as opening off the record. The sign-in page
then saw the cookies and site data of the regular profile and could store
new ones there. Auth Tabs now use an ephemeral profile in every case in
which the browser opens the link off the record: in always-incognito mode,
with the option to open external links in incognito, when the app asks for
an ephemeral tab, and when the app asks for an incognito tab and the
browser accepts the request. The ephemeral profile starts empty and is
discarded when the tab closes, so these sign-in flows start logged out.
Other Auth Tabs keep the regular profile. Auth Tabs only open when custom
tab intents are allowed in the privacy settings; otherwise these links
open in a browser tab.

